'My proposed solution uses the Ultralytics YOLOv8 framework, a state-of-the-art model for object detection and segmentation. I will first leverage the provided `generate_yolo_dataset` method to convert the training and validation datasets into the format required by YOLOv8. Then, I will fine-tune a pre-trained YOLOv8 segmentation model (specifically, `yolov8n-seg.pt` for a fast baseline) on this newly created dataset for a moderate number of epochs. After training, I will use the best-performing model checkpoint to run inference on each image in the validation set. Finally, I will process the model's output masks by resizing them to the original image dimensions and combining them into a single `uint16` instance mask, ensuring that overlapping detections are resolved by giving priority to the instance with the highest confidence score.'
