'My strategy is to use a more powerful model and a more robust training regimen than previous attempts. I will employ the YOLOv8-Large segmentation model (`yolov8l-seg.pt`) and train it on a larger image resolution of 1024x1024 to better capture details of small cells. The training will run for up to 50 epochs with an early stopping patience of 10 to ensure convergence without overfitting while respecting time constraints. After training, the best model checkpoint is used for inference on the validation set. During post-processing, I reconstruct the final instance masks by carefully combining the predicted masks, sorting them by confidence score, and assigning unique instance IDs, ensuring that higher-confidence predictions take precedence in areas of overlap.'
