TION ----------\n            label_path = yolo_label_dir / f"{img_path.stem}.txt"\n\n            if mask_path is not None and Path(mask_path).exists():\n                iou, dice = mask_to_yolo_and_iou(\n                    mask_path=mask_path,\n                    txt_path=label_path,\n                    class_id=class_id,\n                )\n            else:\n                if write_empty_labels:\n                    label_path.touch()\n                else:\n                    continue\n\n            num_written += 1\n\n        # ---------- WRITE data.yaml ----------\n        data_yaml_path = yolo_dir / "data.yaml"\n        yaml_config = {\n            "path": str(yolo_dir.resolve()),\n            "train": "images/train",\n            "val": "images/val",\n            "names": {class_id: class_name},\n        }\n\n        if data_yaml_path.exists():\n            try:\n                with open(data_yaml_path, "r") as f:\n                    existing = yaml.safe_load(f) or {}\n            except Exception:\n                existing = {}\n            existing.update(yaml_config)\n            yaml_config = existing\n\n        with open(data_yaml_path, "w") as f:\n            yaml.safe_dump(yaml_config, f, sort_keys=False)\n\n        self.yolo_dir = yolo_dir\n        self.yolo_yaml_path = str(data_yaml_path)\n\n        print(f"Done. Wrote {num_written} samples to split={split}.")\n        return str(data_yaml_path)\n\n\n    def get_yolo_dataset(self) -> str:\n        if not hasattr(self, "yolo_yaml_path"):\n            raise RuntimeError("YOLO dataset has not been generated yet. Call generate_yolo_dataset(...) first.")\n        return self.yolo_yaml_path\n\ndef collate_fn(batch):\n    imgs, masks, metas = zip(*batch)\n    return list(imgs), list(masks), list(metas)\n```\n\n\n# Previous debugging attempts:\nDesign: My strategy is to use a large, powerful instance segmentation model, `YOLOv8-Large-Seg`, to overcome the failures of previous smaller models. I will prepare the data by converting the provided datasets into the YOLO format using the helper function, ensuring that both training and validation splits are correctly configured. The model will be trained for a significant number of epochs (100) with a large input resolution (1024x1024) to capture fine details of the cells, and I\'ll use early stopping to prevent overfitting and optimize training time. For inference, I\'ll use the best-performing model checkpoint to generate predictions on the validation set. Finally, I will carefully post-process the model\'s output by reconstructing instance masks, resizing them to their original dimensions, and resolving any overlaps by prioritizing predictions with higher confidence scores, which should yield high-quality segmentation results.\nAnalysis: There is a critical bug in the execution. The training script was configured to use the \'yolov8l-seg\' model, train for 100 epochs, and use an image size of 1024. However, the execution log clearly shows that a much smaller \'yolov8n-seg\' model was used, training ran for only 2 epochs, and the image size was 640. This severe mismatch in hyperparameters resulted in a model that did not learn the task, leading to a final SEG score of 0.0.\n\n-------------------------------\nDebug plan: The previous implementation failed because the training parameters for the YOLO model—such as the model size, epoch count, and image resolution—were ignored, causing the system to fall back on weak default settings. This was likely due to a subtle bug in the data loading pipeline that disrupted the trainer\'s configuration process. My solution robustly fixes the `CellSegDataset` class by replacing the fragile filename stem matching with a more reliable integer-based index matching for pairing images and masks. With the data loading stabilized, the specified training parameters (`yolov8l-seg`, 120 epochs, 1024px resolution) will now be correctly applied, leading to a properly trained and effective segmentation model.\nAnalysis: The script exhibits a critical bug where the training parameters specified in the code are completely ignored during execution. The code intended to train a `yolov8l-seg.pt` model for 120 epochs with an image size of 1024. However, the execution log clearly shows that a much smaller `yolov8n-seg.pt` model was trained for only 2 epochs at an image size of 640. This severe undertraining resulted in a model with no meaningful predictive capability, leading to a final SEG score of 0.0. The issue lies in the `ultralytics` training call, which is not correctly parsing or applying the provided arguments.\n\n-------------------------------\nDebug plan: The previous implementation failed because the `ultralytics` training process inexplicably ignored all specified hyperparameters, such as model size, epoch count, and image resolution, and instead fell back to a weak default configuration. This resulted in a severely undertrained `yolov8n-seg` model that was incapable of performing the segmentation task. My solution directly addresses this by explicitly re-stating the desired model, `yolov8l-seg.pt`, within the `.train()` method call itself. This targeted redundancy is designed to forcefully override any faulty default-setting behavior within the library, ensuring the correct large model is used and that all other specified training parameters, such as the 150-epoch duration and 1024px image size, are correctly applied. This will result in a properly trained, high-capacity model capable of achieving accurate cell segmentation.\nAnalysis: There is a bug in the script where the training configuration is being ignored. The code intended to train a `yolov8l-seg` model for 150 epochs at an image size of 1024, but the execution log shows that a `yolov8n-seg` model was trained for only 2 epochs at a size of 640. This severe mismatch in training parameters resulted in a model that failed to learn, achieving a final score of 0.0. The attempted workaround in the `model.train()` call appears to be the source of the issue, causing the trainer to fall back to default settings.\n\n\n\n# Previous (buggy) implementation:\n```python\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport re\nimport yaml\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Dict, Optional\n\nimport cv2\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset\nfrom ultralytics import YOLO\n\n# Helper functions that are assumed to be part of the environment,\n# provided here to make the script self-contained.\n\n\ndef _read_tif_any(path):\n    """Reads a TIF file, handling various formats."""\n    img = cv2.imread(str(path), cv2.IMREAD_UNCHANGED)\n    if img is None:\n        raise IOError(f"Could not read image at {path}")\n    return img\n\n\ndef _as_rgb(img: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    """Converts an image to an 8-bit RGB format."""\n    if img.ndim == 3 and img.shape[2] == 3 and img.dtype == np.uint8:\n        return img\n\n    if img.ndim == 2:\n        img = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_GRAY2RGB)\n    elif img.shape[2] == 1:\n        img = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_GRAY2RGB)\n    elif img.shape[2] == 4:\n        img = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_BGRA2RGB)\n\n    if img.dtype != np.uint8:\n        p_low, p_high = np.percentile(img, (1, 99))\n        if p_high > p_low:\n            img = np.clip((img - p_low) / (p_high - p_low + 1e-6), 0, 1)\n            img = (img * 255).astype(np.uint8)\n        else:\n            max_val = np.max(img) if np.max(img) > 0 else 1.0\n            if max_val > 255:\n                img = (img / (max_val + 1e-6) * 255).astype(np.uint8)\n            else:\n                img = img.astype(np.uint8)\n\n    return img\n\n\ndef _extract_index(stem: str) -> Optional[int]:\n    """Extracts a trailing numeric index from a filename stem."""\n    match = re.search(r"(\\d+)$", stem)\n    if match:\n        return int(match.group(1))\n    return None\n\n\ndef mask_to_yolo(mask_path, txt_path, class_id):\n    """Converts an instance mask to YOLO segmentation format."""\n    mask = _read_tif_any(mask_path)\n    if mask.ndim == 3:\n        mask = mask[..., 0]\n\n    H, W = mask.shape\n    instance_ids = np.unique(mask)\n    instance_ids = instance_ids[instance_ids != 0]\n\n    lines = []\n    for instance_id in instance_ids:\n        instance_mask = (mask == instance_id).astype(np.uint8)\n        contours, _ = cv2.findContours(\n            instance_mask, cv2.RETR_EXTERNAL, cv2.CHAIN_APPROX_SIMPLE\n        )\n\n        if not contours:\n            continue\n\n        contour = max(contours, key=cv2.contourArea)\n        if contour.size < 6:\n            continue\n\n        contour = contour.astype(np.float32).squeeze()\n        if contour.ndim == 1:\n            contour = np.expand_dims(contour, axis=0)\n\n        contour[:, 0] /= W\n        contour[:, 1] /= H\n\n        line = f"{class_id} " + " ".join(f"{coord:.6f}" for coord in contour.flatten())\n        lines.append(line)\n\n    if lines:\n        with open(txt_path, "w") as f:\n            f.write("\\n".join(lines))\n    else:\n        txt_path.touch()\n\n\n# Provided CellSegDataset Class\nclass CellSegDataset(Dataset):\n    """\n    General-purpose segmentation dataset that pairs images and masks by numeric index.\n    """\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        data_dir,\n        ann_dir,\n        split: str = "train",\n        require_masks: bool = True,\n        image_glob: str = "*.tif",\n        mask_glob: str = "*.tif",\n    ):\n        self.data_dir = Path(data_dir)\n        self.ann_dir = Path(ann_dir)\n        self.split = split\n        self.require_masks = require_masks\n\n        self.img_dir = self.data_dir\n        self.mask_dir = self.ann_dir\n\n        img_paths = sorted(self.img_dir.glob(image_glob))\n        if not img_paths:\n            raise RuntimeError(f"No images found in {self.img_dir} (glob={image_glob})")\n\n        mask_paths = sorted(self.mask_dir.glob(mask_glob))\n        if not mask_paths and require_masks:\n            raise RuntimeError(f"No masks found in {self.mask_dir} (glob={mask_glob})")\n\n        img_by_idx: Dict[int, Path] = {}\n        for p in img_paths:\n            idx = _extract_index(p.stem)\n            if idx is not None:\n                img_by_idx[idx] = p\n\n        mask_by_idx: Dict[int, Path] = {}\n        for p in mask_paths:\n            idx = _extract_index(p.stem)\n            if idx is not None:\n                mask_by_idx[idx] = p\n\n        if not img_by_idx:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f"Found images in {self.img_dir} but none matched an index pattern."\n            )\n\n        self.pairs: List[Tuple[int, Path, Optional[Path]]] = []\n        for idx in sorted(img_by_idx.keys()):\n            img_p = img_by_idx[idx]\n            m_p = mask_by_idx.get(idx, None)\n\n            if self.require_masks and m_p is None:\n                print(\n                    f"Warning: Missing mask for image idx={idx}: image={img_p.name}. Skipping."\n                )\n                continue\n\n            self.pairs.append((idx, img_p, m_p))\n\n        if not self.pairs:\n            raise RuntimeError("No (image, mask) pairs could be formed.")\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.pairs)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, i):\n        idx, img_path, mask_path = self.pairs[i]\n\n        img = _read_tif_any(img_path)\n        img = _as_rgb(img)\n\n        mask = None\n        if mask_path is not None:\n            m = _read_tif_any(mask_path)\n            if m.ndim == 3:\n                m = m[..., 0]\n            mask = m.astype(np.uint16)\n\n        meta = {\n            "index": idx,\n            "image_id": img_path.stem,\n            "image_path": str(img_path),\n            "mask_path": str(mask_path) if mask_path is not None else None,\n        }\n        return img, mask, meta\n\n    def generate_yolo_dataset(\n        self, yolo_dir: Path, *, class_id: int = 0, class_name: str = "cell"\n    ) -> str:\n        yolo_image_dir = yolo_dir / "images" / self.split\n        yolo_label_dir = yolo_dir / "labels" / self.split\n        yolo_image_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        yolo_label_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n        print(f"Building YOLO-seg dataset at {yolo_dir} (split={self.split})...")\n        for idx, img_path, mask_path in self.pairs:\n            stem = img_path.stem\n            img = _read_tif_any(img_path)\n            img = _as_rgb(img)\n\n            out_img_path = yolo_image_dir / f"{stem}.png"\n            cv2.imwrite(str(out_img_path), cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_RGB2BGR))\n\n            label_path = yolo_label_dir / f"{stem}.txt"\n            if mask_path and mask_path.exists():\n                mask_to_yolo(mask_path, label_path, class_id)\n            else:\n                label_path.touch()\n\n        data_yaml_path = yolo_dir / "data.yaml"\n        config = {}\n        if data_yaml_path.exists():\n            with open(data_yaml_path, "r") as f:\n                config = yaml.safe_load(f) or {}\n\n        config["path"] = str(yolo_dir.resolve())\n        config["names"] = {class_id: class_name}\n        if self.split == "train":\n            config["train"] = f"images/{self.split}"\n        elif self.split == "val":\n            config["val"] = f"images/{self.split}"\n\n        with open(data_yaml_path, "w") as f:\n            yaml.safe_dump(config, f, sort_keys=False)\n\n        print(f"Done. Wrote {len(self.pairs)} samples to split={self.split}.")\n        return str(data_yaml_path)\n\n\ndef cell_segmentation(\n    train_dataset: CellSegDataset, val_dataset: CellSegDataset\n) -> List[np.ndarray]:\n    """\n    Performs instance segmentation on a validation dataset of cell images.\n    """\n    yolo_data_dir = Path("./yolo_cell_dataset")\n    if yolo_data_dir.exists():\n        shutil.rmtree(yolo_data_dir)\n\n    train_dataset.split = "train"\n    data_yaml_path = train_dataset.generate_yolo_dataset(yolo_data_dir)\n\n    val_dataset.split = "val"\n    val_dataset.generate_yolo_dataset(yolo_data_dir)\n\n    model = YOLO("yolov8l-seg.pt")\n\n    imgsz = 1024\n    batch_size = 4\n    epochs = 150\n    patience = 40\n\n    print("Starting YOLOv8 training with corrected parameters...")\n    # BUGFIX: Explicitly pass the model again in the train call.\n    # This is a workaround for a suspected bug in the ultralytics API where\n    # keyword arguments are ignored unless the model is re-specified, forcing\n    # the trainer to load the correct configuration instead of falling back\n    # to a weak default.\n    model.train(\n        model="yolov8l-seg.pt",\n        data=data_yaml_path,\n        epochs=epochs,\n        imgsz=imgsz,\n        batch=batch_size,\n        patience=patience,\n        project="yolo_runs",\n        name="cell_seg_large_model_final",\n        exist_ok=True,\n        device=0,\n        val=True,\n        seed=42,\n        cos_lr=True,  # Use cosine learning rate scheduler\n        augment=True,  # Enable default augmentations\n    )\n    print("Training finished.")\n\n    best_model_path = Path("yolo_runs/cell_seg_large_model_final/weights/best.pt")\n    if not best_model_path.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError("Could not find trained model weights at \'best.pt\'.")\n\n    predictor = YOLO(best_model_path)\n    val_images = [val_dataset[i][0] for i in range(len(val_dataset))]\n\n    print(f"Running inference on {len(val_images)} validation images...")\n    results = predictor.predict(\n        source=val_images,\n        imgsz=imgsz,\n        conf=0.25,\n        iou=0.6,\n        stream=False,\n        verbose=False,\n    )\n    print("Inference complete.")\n\n    seg_mask_list = []\n    for i, r in enumerate(results):\n        original_img, _, _ = val_dataset[i]\n        original_h, original_w = original_img.shape[:2]\n\n        final_mask = np.zeros((original_h, original_w), dtype=np.uint16)\n\n        if r.masks is None or r.boxes is None or len(r.masks.data) == 0:\n            seg_mask_list.append(final_mask)\n            continue\n\n        confidences = r.boxes.conf.cpu().numpy()\n        sorted_indices = np.argsort(confidences)[::-1]\n        masks = r.masks.data.cpu().numpy()\n\n        instance_id = 1\n        for idx in sorted_indices:\n            mask = masks[idx]\n            resized_mask = cv2.resize(\n                mask, (original_w, original_h), interpolation=cv2.INTER_LINEAR\n            )\n            instance_mask_bool = resized_mask > 0.5\n\n            final_mask[(final_mask == 0) & (instance_mask_bool)] = instance_id\n            instance_id += 1\n            if instance_id > np.iinfo(np.uint16).max:\n                print("Warning: Max instance limit for uint16 reached.")\n                break\n\n        seg_mask_list.append(final_mask)\n\n    print("Post-processing complete. Generated all validation masks.")\n    return seg_mask_list\n\n```\n\n# Execution output:\n```\n✅ Added /work to sys.path\nWorking dir: /\n✅ Added /work to sys.path\nWorking dir: /\n  program_path: /work/program.py (exists: True)\n[INFO] Loading program from /work/program.py\nWARNING ⚠️ user config directory \'/root/.config/Ultralytics\' is not writable, using \'/tmp/Ultralytics\'. Set YOLO_CONFIG_DIR to override.\nCreating new Ultralytics Settings v0.0.6 file ✅ \nView Ultralytics Settings with \'yolo settings\' or at \'/tmp/Ultralytics/settings.json\'\nUpdate Settings with \'yolo settings key=value\', i.e. \'yolo settings runs_dir=path/to/dir\'. For help see https://docs.ultralytics.com/quickstart/#ultralytics-settings.\n[INFO] [SEQ 01] train_data=/work/data/train/01/img\n[INFO] [SEQ 01] train_ann =/work/data/train/01/seg\n[INFO] [SEQ 01] val_data  =/work/data/val/01/img\n[INFO] [SEQ 01] val_ann   =/work/data/val/01/GT/SEG\n[INFO] [SEQ 01] gt_root   =/work/data/val/01/GT\nUsing YOLO dataset directory: /cache/yolo_cellseg\nBuilding YOLO-seg dataset at /cache/yolo_cellseg (split=train)...\nDone. Wrote 172 samples