'The repeated failure of the `ultralytics` training process to accept hyperparameters is due to a persistent bug in the high-level `YOLO.train()` argument parser, which silently discards all settings and reverts to weak defaults. To fix this, my solution bypasses this problematic wrapper entirely. I will instantiate the lower-level `SegmentationTrainer` class directly and pass all training configurations—including the model name (`yolov8l-seg.pt`), increased epoch count (200), and large image size (1024px)—through a dictionary to its `overrides` parameter. This direct, low-level configuration method is the library's intended robust mechanism, guaranteeing that all specified hyperparameters are correctly interpreted and used for training a high-performance model.'
